Fail2Ban Local Configuration File

This document establishes the operational parameters and monitoring directives,

thereby overriding the default configuration settings.

[DEFAULT]

1. Trusted IP Address Exemption (Administrative Access Assurance)

The ignoreip directive is employed to preclude the prohibition of specified

administrative IP addresses. It is imperative that '192.168.29.228' be

accurately replaced with the authorized client's true IP address.

ignoreip = 127.0.0.1/8 192.168.29.228

2. Ban Duration Parameter

The duration of the IP address prohibition is established at 3600 seconds (one hour),

an appropriate tenure for mitigating standard brute-force vectors.

bantime = 3600

3. Maximum Retries Threshold

The maximum permissible count of failed authentication attempts prior to the

implementation of a proactive ban is stringently set to 3.

maxretry = 3

4. Observation Window Duration

This parameter defines the 600-second (10-minute) interval within which the

stipulated maxretry failure count must be achieved.

findtime = 600

----------------------------------------------------

JAILS: Service Monitoring Directives (Zero Trust Mandate)

----------------------------------------------------

5. Secure Shell Daemon (SSHD) Monitoring

Protection mechanisms are enabled for remote Secure Shell authentication attempts,

which is deemed a critical administration vector.

[sshd]
enabled = true

Port 22 is the standard transmission control protocol port for SSH.

port    = ssh
logpath = %(sshd_log)s

6. HTTP Server Monitoring (Contingency Inclusion)

This section remains commented out but serves as a documented contingency for

monitoring web server access logs against high-frequency malicious activity.

#[http-get-dos]
#enabled = true
#port    = http,https
#logpath = %(apache_access_log)s
#maxretry = 100
#findtime = 60